'''tennis†''' (ten′is), ''v. t.'' [< ''tennis'', ''n.''] To drive, as a ball in playing tennis.

{{smaller block|These fowre garrisons issuing foorthe, at such convenient times as they shall have intelligence or espiall upon the enemye, will so drive him from one side to another, and ''tennis'' him amongest them, that he shall finde no where safe to keep his creete [cattle].
{{right|''Spenser'', State of Ireland.}}}}

'''tennis-arm''' (ten′is-ärm), ''n.'' A lameness of tennis-players, said to be caused by a rupture of some of the fibers of the pronator radii teres.

